# Tutorial widget width

`.widgets-grid` is a **single equal-width column**. Every `.widget` in a chapter must share that width. Do not mix a multi-column `auto-fit` grid with one child that spans full width.

```css
/* ✅ same width for Counter, Clock, and every later card */
.widgets-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: 1rem;
}

/* ❌ Counter stays half-width, Clock stretches */
.widgets-grid {
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 24rem), 1fr));
}
.theme-practice-widget {
  grid-column: 1 / -1;
}
```

Nested layouts inside a card (form + history) may use multiple columns. The **cards themselves** may not.
